 "verdict": "ALL 4 certified cross-pair direction books (m5xp/m10xp/m15xp/m30xp) PASS the pre-registered falsifier: badv_persist>0 in EVERY forward year 2024/25/26, all-bars AND bet-tail, CALIBRATED AND RAW -> none is ranking-only; each carries genuine probabilistic skill over a naive trailing-persistence baseline, so no certification downgrades. NUANCE (honest): the persistence baseline is itself WORSE than flat-0.5 (persist_brier 0.252-0.262 > 0.25 => intraday EURUSD direction is mildly ANTI-PERSISTENT), so much of the persistence-advantage is the model avoiding persistence's mistake. Against the HARSHER flat-0.5 baseline the all-bars edge is razor-thin: badv_flat <= +0.0013 (2024 best), shrinks in 2025, and goes slightly NEGATIVE in 2026 for m15xp (-0.00003) and m30xp (-0.00057). The genuine skill is CONCENTRATED IN THE SELECTIVE BET-TAIL (badv_persist_sel +0.005..+0.017), exactly where the books operate via their confidence gate; all-bars Brier dilutes tail skill with the no-skill bulk. Brier-advantage GROWS with horizon (5m ~+0.002 -> 30m ~+0.012 vs persistence), mirroring the known cross-pair edge gradient. CONCLUSION: certifications survive the audit (not ranking-only) but it confirms these are THIN, TAIL-CONCENTRATED, refit-dependent edges; the flat-0.5 margin is ~0 and decaying by 2026 at the long horizons. Audit-only: tightens interpretation, cannot create alpha."
